    "answer": {
      "short": "$A=\\{2,4,6,\\ldots,100\\}$.\n\n$A=\\left\\{x\\in\\mathbb Z\\text{ where }\\frac{x}{2}\\in\\mathbb Z\\text{ and }0<x<101\\right\\}$.",
      "worked": "A roster lists the even-number pattern:\n$$A=\\{2,4,6,\\ldots,100\\}.$$\nIn set-builder notation, $\\frac{x}{2}\\in\\mathbb Z$ requires an even integer, and $0<x<101$ imposes the bounds:\n$$A=\\left\\{x\\in\\mathbb Z\\text{ where }\\frac{x}{2}\\in\\mathbb Z\\text{ and }0<x<101\\right\\}.$$",
